# Source preparation pipeline to be run from mapterhorn/pipelines folder.
# Mosaic of N42/N43 x E141 1-degree Copernicus GLO-30 tiles, cropped to
# lon 141.05-141.85, lat 42.80-43.35 -- generously covering jpsapporo1/
# 5m/10m's own real extent (lon 141.25-141.625, lat 42.917-43.167) on
# every side. Expanded once already this session: the first crop
# (141.10-141.60) missed jpsapporo1's own real east edge (141.625) by
# ~2km, producing empty z16 tiles right at that boundary -- same class
# of mistake as Hakodate's D11/D12, same fix: size the crop to the
# source's own real extent (queried, not guessed), not the originally-
# intended target bbox.
#
# Low-priority global fallback (maxzoom forced down to macrotile_z=12
# by aggregation_covering.py, well below the 1m sources', so it can
# never win their equal-maxzoom tie-break); also serves as a universal
# ~30m land-gap fallback, matching upstream Mapterhorn's own use of
# GLO-30 as its global fallback (both land and sea) -- see
# mapterhorn-japan-bridge's DECISIONS.md D11. Filtered from the full
# source-catalog/glo30 (24,674 global tiles) rather than reusing that
# entry directly, so a bridge run never accidentally pulls the whole
# planet.
[no-cd]
default:
    uv run python source_download.py jpsapporosea
    uv run python source_bounds.py jpsapporosea
    uv run python source_polygonize.py jpsapporosea 4
